{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_4141c7d7e55ca4fdb1910bf3","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"mistral-large-4","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fixed and green.\n\nRoot cause: `billing/currency.py:7` divided by the exchange rate. `NOK_PER_UNIT` in `rates.py` is \"NOK per one unit of foreign currency\", so converting to NOK is a multiplication — `round(amount / 11.50, 2)` turned 10 EUR into 0.87 NOK instead of 115.00. Changed to `amount * nok_per_unit(currency)`.\n\nAlso repaired a missing newline on line 2 of both test files — the tests couldn't even parse before, so the failure was masked by a SyntaxError. That was test-file damage, not the bug; the bug fix itself is only in the billing package.\n\n```\nok   test_mixed_currency_report   (215.0 as expected)\nok   test_nok_only_report         (150.0)\nok   test_nok_line                (100.0)\n```"}],"usage":{"input_tokens":33932,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7d1383e1-dbe0-4fd2-b6d7-148e93784aba","uuid":"d5364a7a-3ed2-4e20-addd-f23af5fd3e2f","timestamp":"2026-10-30T13:13:13.752Z"}
